  "_why": "PATHS_BAND DERIVED INSTEAD OF FLOORED, plus team-derived byes. The band read 12.0 while its own comment described the design as max(12, COIN_FLIP_GAP*4); COIN_FLIP_GAP is 1.0 so the intended value is 4.0 and a hardcoded 12 dominated it — the third floor-over-derivation in this engine after BENCH_CEILING_FLOOR and VALUE_WEIGHT_FLOOR. The composite's top-ten spread runs 7.7 to 40.8 over Cory's twelve picks, so a fixed 12 admitted nearly everything late: at pick 110 it rendered four directions 0.0/0.5/0.7/3.6 behind the top. Now a getter over COIN_FLIP_GAP. Paths rendered across the twelve picks fall 29 -> 20 and every one dropped had a leader 7-12 points behind. ALSO: 564 players carried a team and no bye (37% of top-225 TEs), so byeStack could never count them and its silence was indistinguishable from finding no conflict; all 32 teams show exactly one bye and zero conflicts, so the gaps fill from the player's own team, top-225 goes 33 missing -> 1. Board byte-identical to v12."
